6
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:17,200
Hey.

7
00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:19,700
If you’re going to do that,

8
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:21,100
can you do it somewhere else?

9
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:24,400
The upper floors are a hotel.

10
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:25,650
It has rooms available.

11
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:28,100
Who are you?

12
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,700
This is none of your business.

13
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:31,180
I own this place.

14
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:34,000
If you don’t want to spend the night
at the hotel,

15
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:35,770
do you want to spend time in jail instead?

16
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:45,000
Let’s go.

17
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,100
This is ruining my mood.

18
00:01:48,479 --> 00:01:49,500
You should leave.

19
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:50,600
I’ll see you later.

20
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,360
What? Are you serious?

21
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:55,000
Yes.

22
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:57,100
I don’t want to go with you anymore.

23
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,600
Damn it.

24
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:19,079
Why did you get in the car?

25
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:20,329
I want to be your sugar baby.

26
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:22,900
I want you to adore me.

27
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,200
I’m good at pampering.

28
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:29,200
Please take me.

29
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:31,300
What the hell are you saying?

30
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,480
What are you doing?

31
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:36,600
The other night.

32
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:41,900
When the light went off,
you stopped talking.

33
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,100
I thought…

34
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:47,600
you may prefer it when it’s dark.

35
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,100
You still haven’t told me

36
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:25,600
why you got the moon tattoo.

37
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:51,300
Why are you crying?

38
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,800
2 DAYS AGO.

39
00:05:05,890 --> 00:05:08,210
The renovation on the 11th floor
started today, right?

40
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:09,500
Yes, Miss Chan.

41
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:11,980
The construction will be completed
within seven days.

42
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,550
Remind our staff
that the entire floor is closed.

43
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:17,200
I don’t want guests to stay on the floor
while the construction is ongoing.

44
00:05:17,590 --> 00:05:19,900
Do not cause any noise after 6 p.m.

45
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,170
because it’s time for our guests to rest.

46
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:23,300
Yes, Miss Chan.

47
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:29,880
First impressions are important.

48
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:31,900
Your name tag is also important.

49
00:05:32,090 --> 00:05:33,100
Yes, Miss Chan.

50
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,680
I’m sorry.

51
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:40,760
Miss Chan,
Miss Sun is waiting in your office.

52
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:49,180
Sun.

53
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:53,980
Hello, sister.

54
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,400
Why are you here to see me?

55
00:05:56,730 --> 00:06:00,400
I have to attend a gala party tonight.

56
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:02,380
But I don’t want to go.

57
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:05,050
I’ve been filming for three days straight.

58
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,600
I’m exhausted.

59
00:06:07,850 --> 00:06:08,570
So what?

60
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,770
Can you go to the party as me?

61
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,370
Let’s switch for one day.

62
00:06:12,810 --> 00:06:14,000
Just like we did in high school.

63
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,500
You performed on stage as me.

64
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:18,100
I agreed to do that because you were sick.

65
00:06:18,470 --> 00:06:20,200
That was why I sang on stage.

66
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:25,000
Speaking of singing,

67
00:06:27,350 --> 00:06:29,530
are you not interested in being a singer?

68
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:34,000
When you were young,

69
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:37,010
you said you wanted to be a singer,
and I would be an actress.

70
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,400
No.

71
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,409
I like doing business now.

72
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,900
This is why you are Mom’s favorite.

73
00:06:44,210 --> 00:06:47,100
You do everything
that she wants you to do.

74
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:51,010
So this is all you want to say to me?

75
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:56,000
Actually, I want you
to go to the party with me.

76
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:57,490
Can you go with me?

77
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:59,600
I already booked a seat for you.

78
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,890
You know I don’t like answering the press.

79
00:07:04,230 --> 00:07:07,800
But there will be a lot of pretty girls there.

80
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:08,760
Sun.

81
00:07:11,370 --> 00:07:12,900
You are so stubborn.

82
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:16,780
Fine, I’m leaving.

83
00:07:21,450 --> 00:07:22,300
See you.

84
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:23,700
Bye.

85
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:52,400
I’LL TAKE YOU TO EAT DELICIOUS FOOD.

86
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:06,120
Don’t forget to wake up to eat.

87
00:08:06,150 --> 00:08:07,180
Don’t sleep all day.

88
00:08:08,430 --> 00:08:09,200
I’m leaving.

89
00:08:26,410 --> 00:08:27,930
I’ll have an iced matcha as usual.

90
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,000
Thank you.

91
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:07,800
It’s so good.

92
00:09:12,770 --> 00:09:13,700
So refreshing.

93
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:41,530
Do you have anything to say to me?

94
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:44,760
You are cute.

95
00:09:48,990 --> 00:09:50,090
Are you hitting on me?

96
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:04,250
It’s just a compliment.

97
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:06,900
Thank you.

98
00:10:08,010 --> 00:10:09,210
You are cute too.

99
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:12,500
I know.

100
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,500
Otherwise, you wouldn’t smile at me.

101
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:19,570
I smiled because I’ve never seen anyone
get that excited about food.

102
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:21,900
It tastes really good.

103
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:23,920
Do you want to taste it?

104
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,250
I’ll ask for a new straw.

105
00:10:31,370 --> 00:10:33,100
No, it’s okay.

106
00:10:40,490 --> 00:10:41,500
How is it?

107
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:43,800
Believe me now?

108
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:49,400
Before work,
I always eat something delicious.

109
00:10:50,350 --> 00:10:52,770
I’m a regular customer here.

110
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,700
Their drinks and food are great.

111
00:10:59,130 --> 00:11:01,210
I think I’ll become
a regular customer here too.

112
00:11:04,890 --> 00:11:11,000
Then I hope we will
run into each other often.

113
00:11:14,690 --> 00:11:15,900
What’s your name?

114
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:22,640
I’ll tell you
when we become acquaintances.

115
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:26,800
I hope we will become acquaintances.

116
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:31,000
Do you want another sip?

117
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,900
No, thanks.

118
00:11:35,190 --> 00:11:36,210
I won’t bother you anymore.

119
00:11:45,210 --> 00:11:46,780
Can I have a menu, please?

120
00:12:12,890 --> 00:12:14,210
When you play the intro,

121
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,300
I’ll send you a signal, then you’ll start.

122
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,100
Then the rest of you follow.

123
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,200
Hello, Miss Chan.

124
00:12:37,730 --> 00:12:40,700
Hello, we are The Petal.

125
00:12:41,610 --> 00:12:45,810
This is our first day
performing at the Crescent.

126
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:49,900
I hope you will enjoy our music.

127
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:08,850
♪ It’s late at night,
have you got a ride? ♪

128
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:13,830
♪ If you haven’t, here is my invite ♪

129
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:17,530
♪ Wanna lock eyes a little longer ♪

130
00:13:17,570 --> 00:13:20,200
♪ Can’t let you slip away farther ♪

131
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:25,000
♪ Can we please
spend more time together? ♪

132
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:28,740
♪ The atmosphere’s just right ♪

133
00:13:28,770 --> 00:13:31,180
♪ That we’re here tonight ♪

134
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:35,700
♪ It may be because
I’m talking to you, to you ♪

135
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:38,600
♪ Last two, won’t say goodbye ♪

136
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:41,280
♪ Together, just you and I ♪

137
00:13:41,310 --> 00:13:45,580
♪ It may be because
we feel the same, the same ♪

138
00:13:46,310 --> 00:13:49,900
♪ Even though it’s time to part ♪

139
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:54,200
♪ Still don’t want to be apart ♪

140
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:58,780
♪ It’s late at night,
have you got a ride? ♪

141
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:04,100
♪ If you haven’t, here is my invite ♪

142
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:07,510
♪ Wanna lock eyes a little longer ♪

143
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:10,200
♪ Can’t let you slip away farther ♪

144
00:14:10,390 --> 00:14:14,370
♪ Can we please
spend more time together? ♪

145
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:17,470
♪ Wanna lock eyes a little longer ♪

146
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:20,290
♪ Can’t let you slip away farther ♪

147
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:24,480
♪ Can we please
spend more time together? ♪

148
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,890
I MISS YOU.
CAN YOU GIVE ME ANOTHER CHANCE?

149
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,840
I REALLY WANT TO SEE YOU.

150
00:15:11,170 --> 00:15:12,000
Excuse me.

151
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,440
Are you Sun?

152
00:15:15,310 --> 00:15:17,200
No, I’m her big sister.

153
00:15:18,570 --> 00:15:24,400
So you are Chan, her twin sister?

154
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,000
Yes.

155
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:33,130
This is my first time
meeting twins who are both beautiful.

156
00:15:34,370 --> 00:15:37,500
But I think you look
prettier than your sister.

157
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:41,980
I’m sorry.

158
00:15:43,030 --> 00:15:44,100
I don’t like men.

159
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:46,000
I like women.

160
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:50,000
You are sitting here alone.

161
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:51,900
Don’t you feel lonely?

162
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:54,800
Why don’t we drink together?

163
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:06,700
Have you been waiting long, honey?

164
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:13,500
Do you have something to say
to my girlfriend?

165
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,100
No.

166
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,500
Are you okay?

167
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:33,830
I’m okay. Thank you.

168
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:36,900
Then…

169
00:16:38,350 --> 00:16:40,170
Can you buy me a glass of wine in return?

170
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:45,250
Can I have a glass of wine?

171
00:17:17,859 --> 00:17:19,060
I’m Key.

172
00:17:20,349 --> 00:17:22,000
This is my first day working here.

173
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,089
Nice to meet you.

174
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:28,900
You’re a great singer.

175
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:31,800
Thank you.

176
00:17:35,730 --> 00:17:36,930
Your tattoo.

177
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,300
It’s pretty.

178
00:17:47,890 --> 00:17:49,500
I knew you would like it.

179
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:52,900
I really like it.

180
00:17:54,030 --> 00:17:55,500
Why did you get the moon tattoo?

181
00:17:56,770 --> 00:17:57,810
Is there a particular reason?

182
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:04,600
If you want to know,
you need to come with me.

183
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:09,500
You are quite flirty.

184
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:11,930
Do you use that line a lot?

185
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:17,100
I only use it with you, Chan.

186
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,500
If I go with you,

187
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:33,500
what will I get?

188
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,800
I can give you everything

189
00:18:47,370 --> 00:18:49,000
that makes you happy.

190
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:57,580
Fine.

191
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,700
But only for tonight.

192
00:19:04,090 --> 00:19:05,700
We’ll be together just tonight.

193
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:12,700
What if you are addicted to me?

194
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,700
Are you that good?

195
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:28,780
I like your lipstick.

196
00:19:32,330 --> 00:19:33,580
It makes me want to kiss you.

197
00:19:35,390 --> 00:19:36,500
You want to kiss me?

198
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:39,150
Then do it.

199
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:43,530
Do you dare do it?

200
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:00,400
Why are you so rushed?

201
00:20:01,710 --> 00:20:02,900
What else are you waiting for?

202
00:22:28,130 --> 00:22:29,400
Can you put your hand down?

203
00:22:35,540 --> 00:22:37,800
Try to relax.

204
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:39,730
Be confident and send the energy to me.

205
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:44,200
Be more confident.

206
00:22:45,820 --> 00:22:46,700
Relax.

207
00:22:47,290 --> 00:22:48,900
This brand is about confidence.

208
00:22:49,190 --> 00:22:50,300
Show it.

209
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:01,300
Let’s take a break.

210
00:23:04,700 --> 00:23:05,980
Peach.

211
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:07,730
What’s wrong?

212
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:09,580
Can we change the model?

213
00:23:09,890 --> 00:23:10,730
What?

214
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:14,930
I don’t think she’s the right model
to represent the brand.

215
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:19,200
The concept of this brand is
clothes that give you confidence.

216
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:21,500
The model has no confidence.

217
00:23:21,580 --> 00:23:23,000
We won’t get a good result from her.

218
00:23:23,330 --> 00:23:25,490
The brand specifically chose her.

219
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:28,900
The model personally knows the company.

220
00:23:29,170 --> 00:23:30,700
If you insist on having her,

221
00:23:31,130 --> 00:23:32,380
I can’t continue to work.

222
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:35,850
I’ll send you the contact info
of other photographers.

223
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:37,300
Calm down, Peach.

224
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:41,800
The brand specifically asked for you.

225
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:46,300
How about this?

226
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:49,600
I’ll talk to the model.

227
00:23:55,690 --> 00:23:56,330
Peach.

228
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,400
Key.

229
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,900
When did you get here?

230
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:04,780
I got here
when you were rebuking your client.

231
00:24:04,830 --> 00:24:05,980
You were scary.

232
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:08,770
You don’t need to be scared.

233
00:24:08,970 --> 00:24:10,780
I’m always gentle with you.

234
00:24:11,980 --> 00:24:13,700
Why are you so tough with your client?

235
00:24:13,810 --> 00:24:15,100
Aren’t you afraid of losing them?

236
00:24:15,150 --> 00:24:15,800
No.

237
00:24:16,220 --> 00:24:17,700
I’m not doing this for money.

238
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:19,100
It’s just a hobby.

239
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,530
A hobby?

240
00:24:24,980 --> 00:24:28,200
But you are the go-to photographer
of the top actress.

241
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:29,700
You mean Sun?

242
00:24:30,240 --> 00:24:34,120
We’ve been working together so often
that we’re practically friends.

243
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:42,100
Do you know her twin sister?

244
00:24:43,110 --> 00:24:45,500
I met her a few times.

245
00:24:45,980 --> 00:24:47,570
But I don’t know her personally.

246
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:54,170
I just want to know
if she’s seeing someone.

247
00:24:55,550 --> 00:24:56,810
Has she dated anyone before?

248
00:24:58,560 --> 00:24:59,900
I don’t know.

249
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:03,090
She is hard to approach.

250
00:25:03,860 --> 00:25:05,130
She is very private.

251
00:25:05,550 --> 00:25:07,000
She is totally different from Sun.

252
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:09,400
Why are you asking about her?

253
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:13,000
I’m just curious.

254
00:25:13,580 --> 00:25:14,800
I think she’s pretty.

255
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:21,090
Key.

256
00:25:22,180 --> 00:25:23,300
This Friday.

257
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:26,200
Big Mom wants to hold
a birthday celebration for Dad.

258
00:25:26,390 --> 00:25:27,900
Do you want to go home?

259
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:32,500
They really miss you.

260
00:25:33,050 --> 00:25:34,700
They want you to visit them.

261
00:25:45,940 --> 00:25:48,200
If I don’t have a work schedule, I’ll go.

262
00:25:49,410 --> 00:25:50,200
Fine.

263
00:25:51,610 --> 00:25:53,890
Let me know if you’re coming.

264
00:25:57,520 --> 00:26:01,410
Chan, don’t you think
the quotation is too high?

265
00:26:02,090 --> 00:26:04,700
I’m just renting space
to open an Omakase restaurant.

266
00:26:05,490 --> 00:26:06,900
I’m not renting the entire floor.

267
00:26:07,130 --> 00:26:09,700
You know what kind of hotel
the Crescent is.

268
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:11,890
We always have VIP guests.

269
00:26:12,950 --> 00:26:15,330
The price I offer you is reasonable.

270
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:20,490
I want the quotation for your friend,
not for business partners.

271
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:24,970
When it comes to business,
I don’t consider anyone my friend.

272
00:26:27,660 --> 00:26:29,980
My friend is so ruthless.

273
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:34,700
Why don’t you draft a contract?

274
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:36,400
And we will discuss it again later.

275
00:26:38,470 --> 00:26:41,000
Many people want to open
a restaurant in my hotel.

276
00:26:41,170 --> 00:26:41,980
If you don’t hurry…

277
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:44,300
Fine. I got it.

278
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:45,980
Then do as we’ve agreed on.

279
00:26:46,020 --> 00:26:46,850
Deal.

280
00:26:48,570 --> 00:26:49,440
Deal.

281
00:26:59,740 --> 00:27:04,300
Our college classmates are holding
a reunion party early next month.

282
00:27:04,900 --> 00:27:06,090
Do you want to go with me?

283
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,690
You haven’t seen our friends
from the US for a while.

284
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:13,000
No.

285
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:15,730
Come on. Let’s go together.

286
00:27:16,630 --> 00:27:18,100
I said no.

287
00:27:18,580 --> 00:27:19,700
Stop pestering me.

288
00:28:00,820 --> 00:28:01,800
Simba.

289
00:28:02,230 --> 00:28:03,300
How are you doing?

290
00:28:06,350 --> 00:28:07,200
Are you lonely?

291
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:10,200
Are you still mad at me?

292
00:28:11,530 --> 00:28:13,500
I didn’t come home just one night.

293
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:20,600
He is so mad at me.

294
00:28:38,490 --> 00:28:40,200
It was just one night.

295
00:28:47,270 --> 00:28:48,250
Here is your water.

296
00:29:03,610 --> 00:29:05,200
Why are you so pretty?

297
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:09,100
Your eyes,

298
00:29:09,950 --> 00:29:10,900
your nose,

299
00:29:13,060 --> 00:29:14,170
and your lips.

300
00:29:18,080 --> 00:29:19,100
I’m sorry.

301
00:29:21,140 --> 00:29:22,200
Does it hurt?

302
00:29:25,220 --> 00:29:26,000
No.

303
00:29:26,740 --> 00:29:28,780
I want to know you more.

304
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:32,500
Don’t.

305
00:29:33,390 --> 00:29:36,090
What happens between us
is for tonight only.

306
00:29:38,740 --> 00:29:40,410
Won’t you see me again?

307
00:29:40,860 --> 00:29:41,650
No.

308
00:29:42,870 --> 00:29:44,400
What if we run into each other?

309
00:29:50,240 --> 00:29:51,580
It won’t happen.

310
00:29:58,050 --> 00:30:02,560
Do you know the idiom
‘once in a blue moon’?

311
00:30:04,380 --> 00:30:05,900
It means rarely.

312
00:30:08,820 --> 00:30:13,180
A blue moon doesn’t happen often.

313
00:30:15,990 --> 00:30:17,800
But it doesn’t mean it’s impossible.

314
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:21,280
What are you trying to say?

315
00:30:23,130 --> 00:30:24,800
I’m just saying…

316
00:30:26,020 --> 00:30:28,000
if we run into each other again,

317
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:35,300
it may be because
we are somehow connected.

318
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:38,800
It has nothing to do with it.

319
00:30:39,550 --> 00:30:41,900
What if we run into each other again?

320
00:30:43,620 --> 00:30:45,450
Will you give me a chance?

321
00:30:47,550 --> 00:30:48,400
Sure.

322
00:30:49,330 --> 00:30:51,500
If we run into each other,

323
00:30:52,750 --> 00:30:54,200
I may give you a chance.

324
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:57,900
I guess she really forgot me.

325
00:31:20,300 --> 00:31:22,000
Once in a blue moon?

326
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:28,040
Silly kid.

327
00:31:29,230 --> 00:31:30,500
She was talking nonsense.

328
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:49,100
Hey.

329
00:32:51,150 --> 00:32:52,300
We meet again.

330
00:32:53,900 --> 00:32:54,900
Have a seat.

331
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:04,210
Did you just get here,
or have you already finished your meal?

332
00:33:05,430 --> 00:33:06,700
Are you here alone?

333
00:33:07,710 --> 00:33:08,690
You can sit with me.

334
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:12,600
I finished my meal.

335
00:33:13,230 --> 00:33:14,300
I’m about to leave.

336
00:33:15,260 --> 00:33:20,250
I think we will run into each other often.

337
00:33:26,230 --> 00:33:27,570
You don’t seem to enjoy your meal.

338
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:34,200
The dish is delicious.

339
00:33:36,470 --> 00:33:37,600
I just feel a bit down.

340
00:33:38,300 --> 00:33:39,500
So I don’t want to eat it.

341
00:33:42,990 --> 00:33:44,900
Is something bothering you?

342
00:33:50,510 --> 00:33:53,700
I met someone.

343
00:33:57,480 --> 00:33:58,450
Don’t tell me

344
00:33:59,270 --> 00:34:02,490
a pretty girl like you…
is also going through a breakup?

345
00:34:04,900 --> 00:34:06,730
I can’t even call it a breakup.

346
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:08,929
It’s just a one-night stand.

347
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:11,989
Then you don’t need to care about it.

348
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:14,100
There are many girls out there.

349
00:34:16,699 --> 00:34:18,100
But she…

350
00:34:20,989 --> 00:34:22,650
She is different from other girls.

351
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:30,900
So this one night,

352
00:34:32,580 --> 00:34:34,010
it must be really good.

353
00:34:41,449 --> 00:34:42,400
Okay.

354
00:34:43,460 --> 00:34:45,850
Now I get why you feel down.

355
00:34:47,389 --> 00:34:49,449
I don’t want to end just one night.

356
00:34:56,980 --> 00:35:00,900
Theoretically,
if you think it was a great night,

357
00:35:01,870 --> 00:35:03,610
she probably feels the same.

358
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:11,500
If you were me,

359
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:14,770
what would you do?

360
00:35:19,430 --> 00:35:20,800
If I were you,

361
00:35:24,290 --> 00:35:25,800
I would…

362
00:35:29,130 --> 00:35:30,130
make a move on her.

363
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:34,200
If she was that tasty,

364
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:36,500
I couldn’t let it end
after just one night.

365
00:35:36,540 --> 00:35:37,340
Am I right?

366
00:35:40,410 --> 00:35:41,150
Yes.

367
00:35:42,610 --> 00:35:43,290
Good idea.

368
00:35:47,570 --> 00:35:49,100
We’ve been talking for a while.

369
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:51,010
I still don’t know your name.

370
00:35:55,660 --> 00:35:56,700
What’s your name?

371
00:36:01,550 --> 00:36:02,900
Does it matter?

372
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,930
What if we run into each other often?

373
00:36:07,780 --> 00:36:09,580
Don’t we need to know
each other’s names?

374
00:36:10,590 --> 00:36:12,250
This way our relationship will be unique.

375
00:36:15,620 --> 00:36:16,600
Good.

376
00:36:17,120 --> 00:36:19,100
It’s fun. I like it.

377
00:36:22,990 --> 00:36:24,840
Okay, deal.

378
00:36:25,820 --> 00:36:27,000
We had a good talk today.

379
00:36:27,040 --> 00:36:28,500
I hope to see you again.

380
00:36:31,250 --> 00:36:33,210
Do you want to go grab a drink with me?

381
00:36:33,410 --> 00:36:34,400
Sorry.

382
00:36:35,070 --> 00:36:36,300
I already have a plan.

383
00:36:36,560 --> 00:36:37,730
I’m meeting with my family.

384
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:41,040
Good night.

385
00:36:42,180 --> 00:36:42,930
Good night.

386
00:36:51,140 --> 00:36:51,900
Bye.

387
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:08,500
Do you want anything else?

388
00:37:10,810 --> 00:37:11,930
I have another one of these.

389
00:37:19,770 --> 00:37:20,900
Hello, Miss Chan.

390
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:22,780
Is everything alright?

391
00:37:22,820 --> 00:37:23,600
Yes.

392
00:37:24,260 --> 00:37:25,200
Do you want your usual?

393
00:37:31,540 --> 00:37:32,650
We meet again.

394
00:37:37,290 --> 00:37:38,100
You.

395
00:37:39,430 --> 00:37:40,410
What are you doing here?

396
00:37:41,750 --> 00:37:43,080
I work here.

397
00:37:45,270 --> 00:37:46,770
I work here as a singer.

398
00:37:49,450 --> 00:37:50,300
That’s right.

399
00:37:56,540 --> 00:37:57,750
I told you.

400
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:00,690
We would meet again.

401
00:38:02,650 --> 00:38:04,400
Because I work at your bar.

402
00:38:07,620 --> 00:38:08,970
Why aren’t you working today?

403
00:38:11,230 --> 00:38:12,360
Today is my day off.

404
00:38:14,710 --> 00:38:18,500
But actually, I want to have a side job.

405
00:38:20,180 --> 00:38:22,000
Do you have another job for me?

406
00:38:23,420 --> 00:38:27,570
Especially a job
where I can be close to you.

407
00:38:35,720 --> 00:38:39,700
People who work closely with me
must be good at their job.

408
00:38:41,130 --> 00:38:42,170
Exceptionally good.

409
00:38:47,840 --> 00:38:49,600
Wasn’t I good the other night?

410
00:38:52,350 --> 00:38:53,400
What are you talking about?

411
00:38:53,630 --> 00:38:54,500
So naughty.

412
00:39:04,820 --> 00:39:05,600
Chan.

413
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:10,000
Is this your new friend?

414
00:39:14,650 --> 00:39:15,800
She’s just a silly kid.

415
00:39:16,450 --> 00:39:17,640
Don’t pay attention to her.

416
00:39:30,930 --> 00:39:32,700
I upset the pretty sis.

417
00:39:56,380 --> 00:39:57,410
Are you here alone?

418
00:40:00,100 --> 00:40:00,800
Yes.

419
00:40:04,990 --> 00:40:06,900
Your cocktail looks tasty.

420
00:40:09,050 --> 00:40:10,200
What is the name?

421
00:40:11,590 --> 00:40:13,600
You mean the name of the cocktail?

422
00:40:15,150 --> 00:40:16,400
Or my name?

423
00:40:17,010 --> 00:40:18,400
Both.

424
00:40:21,120 --> 00:40:23,050
But I want to know your name more.

425
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:32,900
Do you want to taste it?

426
00:40:40,230 --> 00:40:41,500
It tastes good.

427
00:40:42,160 --> 00:40:43,900
It tastes good. That should be enough.

428
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:47,500
You don’t need to know the name.

429
00:41:10,710 --> 00:41:11,650
You are so pretty.

430
00:41:12,960 --> 00:41:14,170
Do you really not have a girlfriend?

431
00:41:15,230 --> 00:41:16,500
I don’t like commitment.

432
00:41:17,770 --> 00:41:18,650
Me too.

433
00:41:30,110 --> 00:41:30,650
Hey.

434
00:41:31,970 --> 00:41:33,100
If you’re going to do that,

435
00:41:33,390 --> 00:41:34,780
can you do it somewhere else?

436
00:41:36,580 --> 00:41:37,900
The upper floors are a hotel.

437
00:41:38,330 --> 00:41:39,170
It has rooms available.

438
00:41:43,940 --> 00:41:44,760
Let’s go.

439
00:41:46,120 --> 00:41:46,850
You should leave.

440
00:41:47,450 --> 00:41:48,400
I’ll see you later.

441
00:41:48,450 --> 00:41:49,900
What? Are you serious?

442
00:41:51,870 --> 00:41:52,700
Yes.

443
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:54,770
I don’t want to go with you anymore.

444
00:41:55,210 --> 00:41:56,250
Damn it.

445
00:42:05,390 --> 00:42:06,600
Why did you get in the car?

446
00:42:06,830 --> 00:42:08,530
I have an offer for you, pretty sis.

447
00:42:09,930 --> 00:42:10,770
What is it?

448
00:42:10,940 --> 00:42:12,290
I want to be your sugar baby.

449
00:42:13,290 --> 00:42:14,800
I want you to adore me.

450
00:42:17,650 --> 00:42:18,900
I’m good at pampering.

451
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:21,050
Please take me.

452
00:42:21,820 --> 00:42:23,200
What the hell are you saying?

453
00:42:25,260 --> 00:42:26,330
What are you doing?

454
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:28,500
The other night.

455
00:42:30,090 --> 00:42:33,800
When the light went off,
you stopped talking.

456
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:35,980
I thought…

457
00:42:37,930 --> 00:42:39,500
you may prefer it when it’s dark.

458
00:43:25,630 --> 00:43:27,100
You still haven’t told me

459
00:43:28,580 --> 00:43:30,210
why you got the moon tattoo.

460
00:43:59,500 --> 00:44:02,300
Why are you crying?

461
00:44:13,970 --> 00:44:15,000
I think…

462
00:44:15,960 --> 00:44:17,300
I should go.

463
00:44:18,800 --> 00:44:20,100
I’ll see you.

464
00:44:53,780 --> 00:44:55,180
I’m sorry.

465
00:44:56,570 --> 00:44:58,000
I’m sorry.

466
00:45:01,190 --> 00:45:03,200
I shouldn't have come back.

467
00:46:52,600 --> 00:46:53,300
Aunt Niam.

468
00:46:54,370 --> 00:46:56,000
Good morning, Miss.

469
00:46:56,180 --> 00:47:00,500
I brought a lot of delicious food for you.

470
00:47:01,280 --> 00:47:02,200
Let me help you.

471
00:47:02,220 --> 00:47:04,120
Yes, take this.

472
00:47:04,150 --> 00:47:06,000
Let me take off my shoes first.

473
00:47:10,600 --> 00:47:12,900
Did Dad and Big Mom tell you
to bring it to me?

474
00:47:14,230 --> 00:47:16,780
No one told me to do this.

475
00:47:17,120 --> 00:47:21,000
I made your favorite food.

476
00:47:21,350 --> 00:47:25,730
So I want to give it to you.

477
00:47:29,250 --> 00:47:31,500
Next time, you can have
someone deliver it to me.

478
00:47:31,570 --> 00:47:32,700
How can I do that?

479
00:47:33,040 --> 00:47:34,900
I made the food.

480
00:47:35,150 --> 00:47:37,930
I need to deliver it myself.

481
00:47:39,750 --> 00:47:41,000
Do as you please.

482
00:47:41,520 --> 00:47:42,400
Thank you.

483
00:47:42,850 --> 00:47:43,830
You’re welcome.

484
00:47:43,860 --> 00:47:45,900
I’ll put it in the refrigerator.

485
00:47:54,400 --> 00:47:55,300
Simba.

486
00:47:56,440 --> 00:47:57,250
Come here.

487
00:47:57,510 --> 00:47:58,800
Say hi to Aunt Niam.

488
00:48:02,640 --> 00:48:03,800
Look.

489
00:48:08,710 --> 00:48:11,300
Aunt Niam, you’re doing it again.

490
00:48:12,090 --> 00:48:14,400
I hire a helper
to clean my condo every week.

491
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:16,000
I can’t help it.

492
00:48:16,480 --> 00:48:17,800
This is your condo.

493
00:48:17,990 --> 00:48:21,180
I have to…

494
00:48:21,220 --> 00:48:23,330
…clean it yourself.

495
00:48:24,110 --> 00:48:25,800
Yes, Miss.

496
00:48:29,530 --> 00:48:31,300
I almost forgot.

497
00:48:32,360 --> 00:48:36,040
Madam bought cat treats for Simba.

498
00:48:36,710 --> 00:48:39,100
They are in the brown bag.

499
00:48:40,410 --> 00:48:42,200
I almost forgot it.

500
00:48:42,250 --> 00:48:42,960
Thank you.

501
00:48:42,990 --> 00:48:43,800
Alright.

502
00:48:44,260 --> 00:48:46,800
She must really miss Simba.

503
00:48:47,350 --> 00:48:51,900
Simba is such a cuddly cat.

504
00:48:52,420 --> 00:48:54,400
Who would not fall for it?

505
00:48:55,810 --> 00:48:59,980
How is she doing?

506
00:49:00,670 --> 00:49:02,000
Madam?

507
00:49:02,670 --> 00:49:06,800
She is losing her appetite.

508
00:49:07,460 --> 00:49:08,800
She barely eats.

509
00:49:09,150 --> 00:49:11,400
She also gets sick often.

510
00:49:13,820 --> 00:49:17,500
Dad is probably busy with the farm, right?

511
00:49:27,470 --> 00:49:28,500
Miss Key.

512
00:49:30,440 --> 00:49:34,600
Can’t you find time to visit her?

513
00:49:35,850 --> 00:49:38,010
Although she’s not your biological mom,

514
00:49:38,560 --> 00:49:44,000
she loves you as if you were her daughter.

515
00:49:50,250 --> 00:49:52,690
I can’t go back to that house.

516
00:49:55,430 --> 00:49:58,000
No. Don’t think that.

517
00:49:58,960 --> 00:50:01,370
It happened a long time ago.

518
00:50:02,880 --> 00:50:07,300
It was not your fault.

519
00:50:10,970 --> 00:50:12,130
It was my fault.

520
00:50:13,260 --> 00:50:14,700
It was surely my fault.

521
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:29,900
Stop blaming yourself.

522
00:50:59,660 --> 00:51:02,380
(Why are you crying?)

523
00:51:23,690 --> 00:51:24,700
Shit.

524
00:51:42,760 --> 00:51:43,550
Chan.

525
00:51:46,910 --> 00:51:47,850
I’m sorry.

526
00:51:48,420 --> 00:51:49,850
I’ll call the insurance company.

527
00:51:51,090 --> 00:51:53,000
It’s okay. It’s just a small scratch.

528
00:51:53,650 --> 00:51:54,500
No.

529
00:51:54,840 --> 00:51:55,880
Let’s call the insurance company.

530
00:51:55,920 --> 00:51:57,100
I hit your car.

531
00:51:57,570 --> 00:51:58,780
I need to take responsibility.

532
00:51:59,320 --> 00:52:01,700
After talking to the insurance,
I’ll buy you lunch.

533
00:52:03,440 --> 00:52:05,600
Did you intentionally hit my car?

534
00:52:06,940 --> 00:52:07,800
No way.

535
00:52:08,450 --> 00:52:09,800
Why would I do that?

536
00:52:11,930 --> 00:52:13,130
What are you doing here?

537
00:52:13,910 --> 00:52:15,570
I have a practice with my band.

538
00:52:16,250 --> 00:52:17,770
I didn’t mean to hit your car.

539
00:52:18,350 --> 00:52:19,050
Really?

540
00:52:20,310 --> 00:52:22,170
You always try to get my attention.

541
00:52:26,350 --> 00:52:27,300
That’s true.

542
00:52:28,290 --> 00:52:29,370
I admit it.

543
00:52:30,370 --> 00:52:31,900
I want you to pay attention to me.

544
00:52:32,190 --> 00:52:33,600
But not like this.

545
00:52:35,980 --> 00:52:36,900
You should go.

546
00:52:37,690 --> 00:52:39,000
You don’t need
to take responsibility for it.

547
00:52:40,970 --> 00:52:41,750
Wait.

548
00:52:43,010 --> 00:52:44,700
Since we ran into each other,

549
00:52:45,190 --> 00:52:47,770
why don’t you let me buy you lunch?

550
00:52:49,700 --> 00:52:50,800
As an apology.

551
00:52:51,050 --> 00:52:53,800
No, I don’t need anyone to buy me lunch.

552
00:52:55,500 --> 00:52:57,100
Then can you buy me lunch?

553
00:52:59,030 --> 00:53:00,000
Please.

554
00:53:00,820 --> 00:53:01,600
Please.

555
00:53:11,800 --> 00:53:13,570
Aren’t you going to eat that?

556
00:53:15,430 --> 00:53:16,410
Yes.

557
00:53:17,680 --> 00:53:19,470
But it would be nice
if I could have something else too.

558
00:53:19,510 --> 00:53:22,500
All you think of is that?

559
00:53:22,640 --> 00:53:23,980
All I think of…

560
00:53:24,840 --> 00:53:26,100
…is you

561
00:53:27,260 --> 00:53:28,770
Can you be serious?

562
00:53:30,100 --> 00:53:31,200
I’ll be serious.

563
00:53:32,220 --> 00:53:33,200
So…

564
00:53:34,720 --> 00:53:36,100
did you think about my offer?

565
00:53:38,220 --> 00:53:40,700
Are you interested in having me
as your sugar baby?

566
00:53:41,730 --> 00:53:42,800
Are you sure you’re being serious?

567
00:53:43,070 --> 00:53:44,450
I’m absolutely serious about it.

568
00:53:45,490 --> 00:53:46,500
So?

569
00:53:47,860 --> 00:53:49,100
Are you interested?

570
00:53:51,440 --> 00:53:52,610
I’m a businesswoman.

571
00:53:53,090 --> 00:53:56,600
I don’t make a deal
that doesn’t benefit me.

572
00:54:02,120 --> 00:54:03,580
Then what do you want?

573
00:54:04,990 --> 00:54:06,300
I can give you everything.

574
00:54:07,410 --> 00:54:10,600
I’d do anything for you.

575
00:54:12,260 --> 00:54:13,600
I’ll give in to you in everything.

576
00:54:14,230 --> 00:54:15,400
Just tell me.

577
00:54:17,140 --> 00:54:19,000
A player like you,

578
00:54:20,140 --> 00:54:22,050
how many times
have you made this kind of offer?

579
00:54:23,290 --> 00:54:24,900
You are the first…

580
00:54:26,060 --> 00:54:27,310
and only one.

581
00:54:27,820 --> 00:54:28,600
Really?

582
00:54:29,260 --> 00:54:30,330
What about your other girls?

583
00:54:31,230 --> 00:54:32,700
You seem to have many girls around you.

584
00:54:36,200 --> 00:54:37,500
Don’t worry.

585
00:54:38,710 --> 00:54:43,160
If you take me, I’ll cut them off.

586
00:54:44,040 --> 00:54:45,510
I’ll leave everything behind.

587
00:54:46,650 --> 00:54:48,700
You will have all of me.

588
00:54:49,670 --> 00:54:53,200
And I will have only you.

589
00:54:55,510 --> 00:54:57,000
Why do I have to do that?

590
00:54:57,670 --> 00:55:01,010
I can spend money
on something more useful.

591
00:55:05,920 --> 00:55:09,900
Because we are a good match.

592
00:55:12,970 --> 00:55:14,100
That night,

593
00:55:15,590 --> 00:55:16,900
I fell for you.

594
00:55:18,750 --> 00:55:23,900
You seem to be pretty into me too.

595
00:55:28,130 --> 00:55:29,500
You haven’t told me

596
00:55:30,370 --> 00:55:31,900
why you got the moon tattoo.

597
00:55:37,040 --> 00:55:38,100
How about this?

598
00:55:39,690 --> 00:55:42,900
After finishing lunch, you go to my condo.

599
00:55:43,980 --> 00:55:45,580
I’ll tell you everything.

600
00:55:46,990 --> 00:55:48,100
Tell me now.

601
00:55:49,070 --> 00:55:51,100
I have a cat at home.

602
00:55:53,310 --> 00:55:54,600
Don’t you want to see him?

603
00:55:55,850 --> 00:55:57,470
He’s very cute.

604
00:56:02,090 --> 00:56:04,780
You can hold him, rub his belly,

605
00:56:06,280 --> 00:56:07,500
and even kiss him.

606
00:56:11,630 --> 00:56:12,500
Come in.

607
00:56:24,980 --> 00:56:26,100
Here are the slippers.

608
00:56:42,770 --> 00:56:43,650
Simba.

609
00:56:49,010 --> 00:56:50,000
You can hold him.

610
00:56:50,200 --> 00:56:51,600
He won’t bite or scratch you.

611
00:56:52,150 --> 00:56:53,400
He’s nice just like his owner.

612
00:56:53,850 --> 00:56:54,800
It’s okay.

613
00:56:55,500 --> 00:56:56,900
I’ve never held a cat before.

614
00:56:57,370 --> 00:56:58,290
I don’t know how to do it.

615
00:56:59,080 --> 00:57:02,700
If you are afraid, you can just pat him.

616
00:57:13,290 --> 00:57:14,730
Look, who is this?

617
00:57:19,480 --> 00:57:20,210
Like this.

618
00:57:22,680 --> 00:57:23,570
See?

619
00:57:26,380 --> 00:57:27,580
He’s cute.

620
00:57:33,310 --> 00:57:37,100
I never thought I would be patting a cat.

621
00:57:39,830 --> 00:57:41,200
You already fell for him.

622
00:57:42,730 --> 00:57:44,000
I guess so.

623
00:57:46,570 --> 00:57:48,350
You are cuddling her.

624
00:58:09,800 --> 00:58:11,800
You don’t seem to have a money problem.

625
00:58:13,180 --> 00:58:14,970
Why do you want to be my sugar baby?

626
00:58:21,350 --> 00:58:22,900
I don’t have any money problems.

627
00:58:23,900 --> 00:58:25,600
I just want to be your girl.

628
00:58:31,080 --> 00:58:32,700
Stop being cryptic.

629
00:58:34,540 --> 00:58:35,810
What exactly do you want from me?

630
00:58:44,660 --> 00:58:47,000
Everything is related to this tattoo.

631
00:58:49,520 --> 00:58:50,600
Who are you?

632
00:59:15,490 --> 00:59:17,010
What did Key say, Niam?

633
00:59:17,280 --> 00:59:18,700
Well…

634
00:59:20,230 --> 00:59:21,330
I failed.

635
00:59:23,120 --> 00:59:24,700
She refuses to come home.

636
00:59:25,760 --> 00:59:27,500
Even though she knows you’re sick.

637
00:59:29,130 --> 00:59:32,000
It’s not about that.

638
00:59:32,550 --> 00:59:38,100
I think she still can’t forgive herself about Pin.

639
00:59:44,650 --> 00:59:48,700
This will haunt our family forever.

640
00:59:51,340 --> 00:59:55,650
I feel sorry for Key
for what she’s going through.

641
01:00:00,380 --> 01:00:02,200
Kiran Mahattanakit.

642
01:00:02,750 --> 01:00:06,600
Your last name is Mahattanakit,
but you work as a singer at my bar?

643
01:00:11,720 --> 01:00:13,300
I want to be close…

644
01:00:14,040 --> 01:00:16,000
to the person who saved my life.

645
01:00:22,440 --> 01:00:24,700
The person who is my first love.

646
01:00:27,220 --> 01:00:28,050
Hold on.

647
01:00:29,980 --> 01:00:31,500
Have we met before?

648
01:00:36,920 --> 01:00:41,600
I won’t tell you if we have met.

649
01:00:45,720 --> 01:00:47,450
You have to remember it yourself.

650
01:01:05,210 --> 01:01:06,700
But I can tell you this.

651
01:01:09,290 --> 01:01:11,400
I chose to get the moon tattoo
because of you.

652
01:01:14,060 --> 01:01:15,700
You are my first love.

653
01:01:36,040 --> 01:01:38,100
As long as I can be with you,

654
01:01:41,570 --> 01:01:43,200
it doesn’t matter what I am to you.

655
01:01:45,860 --> 01:01:47,150
I’ll accept it.

656
01:02:20,130 --> 01:02:22,170
Why do you want to be my sugar baby?

657
01:02:22,510 --> 01:02:23,500
It seems fun.

658
01:02:23,930 --> 01:02:27,410
So she and you are not
just a one-night stand anymore.

659
01:02:27,870 --> 01:02:28,780
I have a new rule.

660
01:02:29,020 --> 01:02:31,560
The two of us will not kiss.

661
01:02:33,680 --> 01:02:34,670
What song is this?

662
01:02:34,710 --> 01:02:36,300
It’s a song that I wrote.

663
01:02:36,700 --> 01:02:37,600
It sounds great.

664
01:02:38,180 --> 01:02:39,100
Sing it again.

665
01:02:39,720 --> 01:02:41,090
You don’t need to pretend, Jay.

666
01:02:41,620 --> 01:02:43,000
I know you hate me.

667
01:02:43,290 --> 01:02:44,970
I just want to take what is mine back.

668
01:02:48,390 --> 01:02:51,580
You have no right to touch my stuff,
especially this piano.

669
01:02:52,730 --> 01:02:53,600
Hi.

670
01:02:54,280 --> 01:02:55,250
Do you miss me?
